From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:03:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: IR strobe GPIO and ir:flash-23

Stage C device tree changes:

 - camera@10 (VD55G0) gets st,leds = <1>: sensor GPIO 1 is the strobe output
   (Windows writes 0x0468 = 0x02). The vd55g driver ignores it unless its
   module parameter illuminator=1, which only the IR test boot sets (0094). No
   leds link and no led-names: the driver never drives the PMIC.
 - a second ganged IR LED, ir:flash-23 (flash channels 2 and 3, Windows'
   "LED2"), for the electrical decode check T0b: it has the same limits and
   gates as ir:flash-14 (100 mA per channel at most, 10 ms hardware timer,
   color IR so torch is refused, binds only with ir_test=1), and the channels
   are disjoint from ir:flash-14. Nothing is expected to be connected to it; a
   software strobe should report both channels as open circuit (STATUS1 0x28),
   which cross-checks how the 0x82 of channels 1 and 4 is read.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
index ee13b596ba40..0ff200622136 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
@@ -82,17 +82,20 @@ &cci0_i2c0 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;

 	/*
-	 * IR camera, ST VD55G0 (ACPI CAMI, SMO55F0 / MSHW0472). Probe and
-	 * stream only: the illuminator is not connected. There is no `st,leds`
-	 * (the driver then keeps every sensor GPIO off) and no `leds = <...>`
-	 * link to a flash LED.
+	 * IR camera, ST VD55G0 (ACPI CAMI, SMO55F0 / MSHW0472). `st,leds = <1>`
+	 * names sensor GPIO 1 as the strobe output (Windows writes 0x0468 = 0x02),
+	 * but the vd55g driver honours it only with its module parameter
+	 * illuminator=1, which the omarchy-surface-sl7 modprobe rule sets on the
+	 * "linux-sl7 (IR test)" boot entry alone (patch "vd55g: illuminator").
+	 * On every other boot the property is ignored: no GPIO is a strobe output
+	 * and there is no led_mode control. There is no `leds = <...>` link to a
+	 * flash LED and no led-names: the driver never drives the PMIC.
 	 *
-	 * The illuminator is the PM8550 flash (QCOM0C27, 700 mA) but its
-	 * channel is probably 1 and 4 together. The ganged test LED under
-	 * &pm8550_flash below is test-only and binds to nothing from this node.
-	 * Do not add a `leds = <...>` link until the channel has been found on
-	 * the device
-	 * (see the Phase B notes). Never drive it as a continuous torch.
+	 * The illuminator is the PM8550 flash (QCOM0C27, 700 mA), probably
+	 * channels 1 and 4 together. The ganged test LED under &pm8550_flash
+	 * below is test-only and binds to nothing from this node. Do not add a
+	 * `leds = <...>` link until stage C has settled the wiring. Never drive
+	 * it as a continuous torch.
 	 *
 	 * The master clock is unknown: no SL7 resource file names one. MCLK0
 	 * (gpio96) at 19.2 MHz is the first guess; the vd55g module
@@ -117,6 +120,9 @@ camera@10 {

 		orientation = <0>; /* front facing */

+		/* GPIO 1 is the strobe output; ignored unless vd55g.illuminator=1 */
+		st,leds = <1>;
+
 		vcore-supply = <&vreg_l2m_1p2>;
 		vddio-supply = <&vreg_l4m_1p8>;
 		vana-supply = <&vreg_l6m_1p8>;
@@ -210,6 +216,22 @@ led-0 {
 		flash-max-microamp = <200000>;
 		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Stage C electrical decode check (T0b): channels 2 and 3 ganged, the
+	 * other pair of the module (Windows' "LED2"). Same limits and gates as
+	 * ir:flash-14, IR test boot only; nothing is expected to be connected
+	 * to them, a software strobe should report both as open circuit.
+	 */
+	led-1 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
+		function-enumerator = <23>;
+		led-sources = <2>, <3>;
+		led-max-microamp = <10000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <200000>;
+		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
+	};
 };

 &spi10 {
